==Acquisition==
The mod can be bought from [[Master Teasonai]] for {{sc|20,000}} after reaching '''Rank 3 - Trusted''' with the [[Ostron]]s.


== Notes ==

* Companion Ability cooldown reduction can be triggered by the player or companion killing enemies affected by 3 or more unique Status Effects.
* When a Companion uses a Precept that hits an enemy, all [[Damage#Damage_Types|Damage Types]], modded or innate, are inflicted as Status Effects on the enemy at one stack.
** For example, a MOA is equipped with {{M|Shockwave Actuators}} and a {{Weapon|Deth Machine Rifle}} modded for {{D|Gas}} and {{D|Cold}}. When it uses Shockwave Actuators, all enemies hit by the shockwave are inflicted with one stack of {{D|Gas}}, {{D|Cold}}, {{D|Impact}}, {{D|Puncture}}, and {{D|Slash}}.
** Only whether an element is on the weapon is taken into account, not weighting or status duration. Mods such as {{M|Lasting Sting}} have no effect.
** Elements generated via {{M|Momentous Bond}} will also apply to Companion Precepts.
* Requires Precepts to deal damage or apply status in order to trigger the companion weapon's status effects - this excludes Precepts that affect enemies in other ways, such as {{M|Cordon}}, while Precepts with delayed damage such as {{M|Fatal Attraction}} or {{M|Anti-Grav Grenade}} will likewise only trigger status application on the damage instance.
** Not all damaging Precepts mention dealing any damaging hits in their descriptions; these include {{M|Whiplash Mine}}, {{M|Shockwave Actuators}}, and {{M|Repo Audit}}.
** Precepts that apply innate status without dealing damage include {{M|Coolant Leak}} and {{M|Electro Pulse}}.
* Applied status effects that can deal damage are not affected by mods or the base damage of the companion weapon. They will deal 1 damage per damage tick.
** Due to the [[Heat_Damage#Heat_Inherit|Heat Inherit]] mechanic, when utilizing Heat based weaponry, it is not recommended to mod {{D|Heat}} on your companion weapon as to avoid lowering your Heat DoT output if your companion precepts inflict Heat before you.
*** This may be beneficial when using {{M|Contagious Bond}} because if the first heat proc is from a companion all subsequent heat procs will be counted as damage from that companion.
*** However, despite only adding{{D|Heat}} damage of weapon hits, the increased {{D|Heat}} from {{M|Fired Up}} can be [[Heat Inherit|Heat Inherited]] from applied procs from abilities.
** [[Faction Damage Mods]] are still applied once if applied on a target with a heat proc from Manifold Bond
* Works with every hit of [[Eximus]] auras copied by {{M|Null Audit}}.
* The cooldown reduction of companion abilities does '''not''' include:
** The cooldown on cloaking on {{M|Ghost}} from {{Companion|Shade}}.
* Manifold Bond will trigger on {{WF|Wisp}} {{A|Reservoirs}} Shock Mote.

